  "issue": "### Issue with CSharpLexer Keyword Recognition\n\nHello maintainers,\n\nI've encountered an issue with the `CSharpLexer` in the Pygments library after a recent update. It seems that the lexer is not correctly recognizing certain keywords, which is causing unexpected behavior during syntax highlighting.\n\n### Description\n\nThe problem arises when using the `CSharpLexer` to parse C# code that includes certain contextual keywords. Specifically, the lexer fails to properly identify and highlight the keyword `file` when it is used in certain contexts, such as with class modifiers. This results in incorrect syntax highlighting, which can be misleading for users relying on accurate code representation.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create a C# file with the following content:\n   ```csharp\n   file class ExampleClass\n   {\n       // Some code here\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. Use the `CSharpLexer` to parse the file and observe the syntax highlighting.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe keyword `file` should be highlighted correctly as a keyword when used as a class modifier.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nThe keyword `file` is not recognized and highlighted correctly, leading to inconsistent syntax highlighting.\n\n### Additional Information\n\nThis issue seems to have been introduced in a recent change to the lexer. It would be great if this could be addressed to ensure accurate syntax highlighting for C# code.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter!",
